    "title": "Recent rains delay Highway 2 project completion - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mike Peterson ,\n15 hours ago (Shenandoah) -- Iowa Department of Transportation officials say it'll be the end of this month before a portion of Highway 2 in Fremont County is reopened to traffic. DOT officials closed the highway between County Roads L-68 and L-40 in April to allow for extensive repairs from the floods of 2011 and 2019. Plans originally called for 2 to reopen in September. Scott Suhr is the DOT's District 4 planner. Under a revised timeline, Suhr tells KMA News the project won't be finished and the highway reopened until October 29. Read full article",
    "summary": "15 hours ago (Shenandoah) -- Iowa Department of Transportation officials say it'll be the end of this month before a portion of Highway 2 in Fremont County is reopened to traffic. DOT officials closed the highway between County Roads L-68 and L-40 in April to allow for extensive repairs from the floods of 2011 and 2019. Plans originally called for 2 to reopen in September. Scott Suhr is the DOT's District 4 planner. Under a revised timeline, Suhr tells KMA News the project won't be finished and the highway reopened until October 29.",
